; ===========================================================================
;  sprites.tiles -- the dino, the pterodactyl and the clouds
; ===========================================================================
;  Colour 0 is transparent in a sprite, so a '.' inside the dino's outline is
;  a hole the background shows through.  That is how the eye is drawn: it
;  costs no colour, and it inverts for free when the palette flips to night.
;
;  The dino is 24x24 standing and 32x16 ducking, which is the same 44x47 to
;  59x30 proportion the browser's is.  Its feet sit on y=192.
; ===========================================================================

@bank spr

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  $00  standing still, and also the pose held for the whole of a jump
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
@sprite DINO_STAND $00 3x3
.............ooooooooo..
